            <ArticleTitle>[Study on the safety after cesarean section].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>225-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">In order to assess the safety after cesarean section, the complications and morbidity rate within 2 years after delivery between cesarean section and spontaneous delivery were compared.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A retrospective cohort study was used in this study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The prevalence of anemia, mobility restriction of uterus, chronic pelvic pain and wound ache during the 2 years postpartum in cesarean section group were 11.1%, 9.6%, 4.3% and 5.1% respectively, which were significantly higher than those in women with spontaneous delivery.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">In order to protect women's health, the indications for cesarean section must be mastered strictly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
